The optional current test weights are the AWQ quantization published as
stelterlab/Mistral-Small-24B-Instruct-2501-AWQ, derived from Mistral Small 24B.
The model card declares Apache-2.0. The exact quantized revision and the
historical Mistral BF16 baseline revision are recorded in
pins/nightly-2026-07-28.json. Model weights are downloaded directly from
Hugging Face and are not distributed by this repository.

The Qwen3.8-27B BF16 benchmark used Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B revision
1d4bf0f2ff6012fd82039f2fa52739d0dd7c60c0. Its model card declares
Apache-2.0. Those weights were deleted after the benchmark and are not
distributed by this repository.

The current Qwen3.8-27B W4A16 benchmark uses
abihsoro/Qwen3.8-27B-AWQ-INT4 revision
f2e0cac39907e7b1ed7fdb210363dd33cc18f993. The DFlash2 compatibility test uses
z-lab/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2 revision
50307d4c4cde6860d4eee73e2547cd786fe8e8a4. Their model cards declare
Apache-2.0. Both are downloaded directly to local storage, retain their target
model attribution, and are not distributed by this repository.

Ling 3.0 support was ported from InclusionAI's public vLLM support branch and
subsequent vLLM commits recorded in pins/nightly-2026-07-28.json. Optional
inclusionAI/Ling-3.0-tiny BF16, FP8, and INT4 repositories declare the MIT
License. The pinned BF16 weights were downloaded only to local storage for
real-weight benchmarking; model weights are not distributed by this repository.

The Windows ROCm Triton MLA prefill fallback is original integration code by
Carlo Pasquale, Copyright 2026, distributed under Apache-2.0 as part of this
project. It modifies the Apache-2.0 vLLM source tree through a clearly named,
version-locked patch and retains vLLM's upstream notices.

The dynamic compile-range dispatcher correction and its regression test are
also original Carlo Pasquale project contributions distributed under
Apache-2.0 in a separate, clearly named version-locked patch.
